{'symbol': 'AWK', 'date': '2023-06-20 16:43:00', 'title': 'ILLINOIS AMERICAN WATER ACQUIRES VILLAGE OF TOLONO WATER AND WASTEWATER SYSTEMS', 'text': "TOLONO, ILL.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--ILLINOIS AMERICAN WATER, A SUBSIDIARY OF AMERICAN WATER, ANNOUNCED TODAY THE ACQUISITION OF THE VILLAGE OF TOLONO WATER AND WASTEWATER SYSTEMS FOR $9.416 MILLION. THE NEWLY ACQUIRED SYSTEMS ADD APPROXIMATELY 1,295 WATER AND 1,254 WASTEWATER CUSTOMERS TO THE COMPANY'S EASTERN ILLINOIS SERVICE AREA. “OUR TEAM IS EXCITED TO EXPAND OUR SERVICES AND DIRECTLY SERVE OUR NEW CUSTOMERS IN TOLONO,” SAID REBECCA LOSLI, PRESIDENT OF ILLINOIS AMERICAN WATER. “SINCE 2020 WE HAV."}